  "analysis": "Both responses outline a multi‑lane plan, gating, approvals, and rollback procedures that respect the repository constraints. TGM gives a clear three‑lane structure and focuses on local and staging verification, but it is less explicit about the idempotency contract, race‑condition safety, and cost‑control of integration runs. HWF adds a specification lane defining the idempotency key, includes a security review for race conditions, emphasizes immutable config injection, and explicitly limits integration suite executions to save compute credits, addressing more of the requester’s risk concerns.",
